{{feat
|type=class
|prereq=[[bard]]
|desc=Bards are able to sing a song that can bolster their allies. [[Deaf]]ened [[creature]]s are not affected by the bard's singing. The song affects all allies within 30 feet and lasts for 10 [[round]]s. The higher the bard's final [[perform]] skill and class level, the better the bard song.
|use=selected
|icon=ife_bardsong.gif
|class1=bard
}}

== Notes ==

*This feat may be used once per [[bard]] level per day.
* A ''bard song'' cannot be started while [[silence]]d, nor will it affect silenced creatures.
* Depending on the power of the song, a ''bard song ''can provide bonuses to [[attack roll]]s, damage rolls, each type of [[saving throw]] (fortitude, reflex, and will), [[armor class]] (AC, specifically a [[dodge bonus]]), and [[skill]]s. It can also provide [[temporary hit point]]s (THP).
**The damage bonus is listed on the character sheet as bludgeoning. However the actual damage is the type of the weapon wielded.
*This feat has no effect on characters currently influenced by a bard song (excluding [[curse song]]s). A bard should be aware of this if starting a new song before an old one expires.
*The feat [[lingering song]] increases the duration by 5 rounds (15 rounds total). The feat [[lasting inspiration]] increases the duration 10 times (100 rounds total). They [[stack]], but lasting inspiration is applied first; so, with both feats, the duration is 105 rounds.
**Other feats that may be of interest to someone using ''bard song'' include [[extra music]] and [[curse song]].
*This ability can be used while [[polymorph]]ed.
*The bonus to attack provided by this ability counts towards the +20 [[attack bonus cap]].
*The bonus to saving throws provided by this ability counts towards the +20 saving throw bonus cap.
*The bonus to skills provided by this ability counts towards the +50 skill bonus cap.
*The perform skill required for the highest levels of bard song is unattainable without magic items.

